Spring Bean Life cycle
=====================
Bean Life Cycle:
Instantiate → Inject → Aware → Before Init → Initialize → After Init → Use → Destroy

1. Instantiate
Spring creates the bean object using constructor.

2. Inject
Spring injects all dependencies (@Autowired, setters, constructors).

3. Aware
Spring provides context info if bean implements Aware interfaces.

4. Before Init
Spring runs BeanPostProcessor before initialization.

5. Initialize
Custom initialization logic runs (@PostConstruct, init methods).

 @PostConstruct
    public void init() {
        System.out.println("DB connected");
    }

       @PostConstruct
public void loadCache() {
    users = userRepository.findAll();
}


6. After Init
Spring applies proxies (AOP, transactions, security).

7. Use
Bean is fully ready and serves application requests.

  @PreDestroy
    public void close() {
        System.out.println("DB connection closed");
    }

     @PreDestroy
     public void shutdownPool() {
     executorService.shutdown();
}

8. Destroy
Spring cleans resources before shutting down (@PreDestroy).


Example 
@Component
public class DBService {

    @PostConstruct
    public void init() {
        System.out.println("DB connected");
    }

       @PostConstruct
public void loadCache() {
    users = userRepository.findAll();
}



  


}
